    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (there's a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, plus the `AcceptanceBase` helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule while keeping the logic well-factored:\n\n1. **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `countOwnersInHousehold(String householdId)`, mirroring the existing `countOwnersInCity` / `countOwnersRegisteredOn` count methods (the household-size query belongs in the service/persistence layer).\n\n2. **New `MembershipTierEvaluator`** (in the `service` package) \u2014 a small single-responsibility component that owns the *entire* tier decision. It returns `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members, and otherwise applies the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules. This follows the established `BulkSignupWarningEvaluator` pattern (a `@Component` injected into the mapper that queries `ClinicService`).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 moved the BRONZE/SILVER logic out of the mapper's `formatMembershipTier` method (deleted) and now delegates the `membershipTier` mapping to the injected `membershipTierEvaluator.tierFor(owner)`, keeping the mapper thin and consistent with how `bulkSignupWarning` is handled.\n\nThe GOLD check guards against a null/blank `householdId` (an owner not in a shared household never counts as GOLD), so BRONZE/SILVER behavior for ordinary owners is unchanged.",
